m is listed with movie title, screening date, time, row number, seat description and price.\n- [ ] AC-37 — A couch is described as `Couch <a>-<b>`; a single seat is described by its column number.\n- [ ] AC-38 — The total line reads `Total: <sum> PLN` and equals the sum of the listed prices.\n- [ ] AC-39 — `Back` returns to the seat map with the selection intact.\n- [ ] AC-40 — `Confirm` navigates to `/screenings/:id/checkout`.\n- [ ] AC-59 — The summary shows the title `Your tickets`.\n- [ ] AC-60 — Each summary item has a `Remove` button that removes it from the booking and updates the total; removing the last item returns to the seat map.\n- [ ] AC-67 — Every summary identifier in section 9.3 is present with the exact names and values given there.\n- [ ] The booking survives a reload of the seat map and of the summary.\n\n==== spec/tickets/05-checkout.md\n# 05: Checkout and payment\n\n**What to build:** The customer fills in their details on the checkout form (`Your details`), sees validation messages as they go, can go `Back` to the summary and return — or reload — without losing what they typed, and pays with the `Pay <total> PLN` button. Paying sends the reservation to the backend; success opens `/confirmation`, failure keeps the form and shows a toast.\n\n**Specification:** sections 2.1, 2.2 (`POST /reservations`), 3.1, 7, 9.4, 9.7.\n\n**Blocked by:** 04 — Booking and summary.\n\n**Status:** ready\n\n- [ ] AC-41 — The form renders first name, last name, email, confirm email, phone number and a terms checkbox.\n- [ ] AC-42 — First name and last name are required and must be at least 2 characters.\n- [ ] AC-43 — Email is required and must be a valid address; confirm email must match it.\n- [ ] AC-44 — Phone number is optional; when filled it must be exactly 9 digits.\n- [ ] AC-45 — The terms checkbox is required.\n- [ ] AC-46 — The pay button is enabled whenever no payment request is in flight; clicking it on an invalid form marks all fields as touched, shows the messages and shows the toast `The form contains errors`, without navigating.\n- [ ] AC-47 — The pay button on a valid form sends `POST /reservations`, is disabled while the request is in flight, navigates to `/confirmation` on success, and on failure stays on the form and shows the toast `Payment failed. Please try again.`\n- [ ] AC-61 — The checkout shows the title `Your details`.\n- [ ] AC-62 — The pay button reads `Pay <total> PLN`, the total of the booking.\n- [ ] AC-63 — `Back` on the checkout returns to the summary with the booking intact.\n- [ ] AC-64 — The checkout values survive going back to the summary and forward again, and a page reload; a new booking starts with an empty form.\n- [ ] AC-65 — The labels of the five required fields end with `*`; the phone label does not.\n- [ ] AC-68 — Every checkout identifier in section 9.4 is present with the exact names and values given there.\n\n==== spec/tickets/06-confirmation.md\n# 06: Confirmation and booking lifecycle\n\n**What to build:** After a successful payment the customer sees the confirmation with their email address; `Continue` clears the booking and returns to `/`. The whole booking lifecycle from section 3.1 holds: it survives reloads, and every route guards against a missing or mismatched booking.\n\n**Specification:** sections 3.1, 8, 9.5.\n\n**Blocked by:** 05 — Checkout and payment.\n\n**Status:** ready\n\n- [ ] AC-48 — `/confirmation` shows `Payment successful` and `Your tickets will be sent shortly to <email>`; `Continue` navigates to `/` and clears the booking; the booking survives a reload via `sessionStorage`; entering the summary, checkout or confirmation without a matching booking redirects to `/`.\n- [ ] AC-69 — Every confirmation identifier in section 9.5 is present with the exact names and values given there.\n- [ ] Reloading `/confirmation` after paying still shows the confirmation.\n- [ ] After `Continue`, the seat map of the same screening shows no selected seats and the checkout form of a new booking is empty.\n\n==== spec/tickets/07-final-pass.md\n# 07: Final pass\n\n**What to build:** A walk through the whole flow — movie list, seat map, summary, checkout,\nconfirmation — against the specification, fixing whatever does not match.\n\n**Specification:** the whole of `README.md`, section 9 in particular.\n\n**Blocked by:** 01–06.\n\n**Status:** ready\n\n- [ ] Every acceptance criterion in section 10 is met.\n- [ ] `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds.\n\n==== spec/tickets/README.md\n# Tickets\n\nWork through the tickets in order. A ticket can start once every ticket in its\n**Blocked by** line is done. The specification is [`../README.md`](../README.md); each\nticket names the sections it implements and the acceptance criteria it must satisfy.\n\n| # | Ticket | Blocked by | Criteria |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 01 | [Movie list and day picker](01-movie-list.md) | — | 11 |\n| 02 | [Auditorium map](02-auditorium-map.md) | 01 | 13 |\n| 03 | [Seat selection, legend and selected-seats panel](03-seat-selection.md) | 02 | 14 |\n| 04 | [Booking and summary](04-booking-summary.md) | 03 | 16 |\n| 05 | [Checkout and payment](05-checkout.md) | 04 | 13 |\n| 06 | [Confirmation and booking lifecycle](06-confirmation.md) | 05 | 2 |\n| 07 | [Final pass](07-final-pass.md) | 01–06 | all |\n\nA ticket is done when every box in it is ticked and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
