{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Build the Cinescope cinema seat-booking web application described in spec/README.md as the Angular 22 app `cinescope` (apps/cinescope) in this Nx workspace, following spec/stack.md. Implement the seven tickets in spec/tickets/ (01 movie list, 02 auditorium map, 03 seat selection, 04 booking and summary, 05 checkout, 06 confirmation and booking lifecycle, 07 final pass) in order. Do not ask questions; where the spec is silent, choose the simplest option that satisfies it. Finish only when every ticket is done (all boxes ticked) and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds. Commits were not requested; do not commit unless asked.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Angular 22 standalone components, zoneless, Angular Router with withComponentInputBinding (route params and `date` query param bound to input()), SCSS, signals and computed.\n   - HttpClient (provideHttpClient) against json-server 0.17.4 at http://localhost:3000; POST /reservations.\n   - Angular Material 22: MatDatepickerModule (matDatepicker, [min], [value], dateChange), MatSnackBar (toast; a new open dismisses the previous one), MatButton (mat-flat-button / mat-stroked-button), MatFormField/MatInput, MatCheckbox, provideNativeDateAdapter.\n   - Reactive forms planned for checkout; sessionStorage-backed BookingService planned.\n   - Nx 23 with pnpm 11.1.0; Node 26.5.0.\n   - Browser verification via a hand-rolled Chrome DevTools Protocol client (Node global WebSocket) against headless Chromium from /opt/ms-playwright.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - spec/README.md, spec/stack.md, spec/tickets/01–07*.md and spec/tickets/README.md: read in full. Key spec points: data-testid contract (section 9), acceptance criteria (section 10), routes (section 3), colours and prices (5.3, 5.4), validation rules (7).\n   - db.json: backend data (5 movies, 26 screenings across 15–21 Sep 2026, reservations: []). Must not be hand-edited. Testing POSTs will append to it; restore with git checkout if changed by tests.\n   - apps/cinescope/src/app/models.ts (created): Movie, Screening, CustomerDetails, NewReservation, Reservation (extends NewReservation with id).\n   - apps/cinescope/src/app/api.ts (created): CinemaApi service with movies(), movie(id), screenings(), screening(id), createReservation(reservation); BASE_URL = 'http://localhost:3000'.\n   - apps/cinescope/src/app/dates.ts (created): WEEKDAYS, startOfToday(), addDays(), toIsoDate(), parseIsoDate() (returns null for invalid/non-existent dates), formatShowDate(isoDate, time).\n   - apps/cinescope/src/app/movie-list/movie-list.ts (created): MovieList component. Key parts: `date = input<string>()`; `minDate = startOfToday()`; `days` (Today + 4 weekday labels); `selectedDate` computed (valid ISO and >= today, else today); `dayButtons`, `pickerValue`; `loading`, `failed`, `catalogue` signals; forkJoin of movies and screenings on construct and on load() (Retry); `cards` computed (movies in backend order with that day's screenings sorted by time, filtered to non-empty); `selectDay(iso)` navigates with queryParams {date}; `onDatePicked(value)` ignores dates before today; `openSeats(id)` navigates to /screenings/:id/seats.\n   - apps/cinescope/src/app/movie-list/movie-list.html (created): day-picker section with day buttons (data-testid day-button, data-date, data-selected via [attr.data-selected]) and mat-form-field with input data-testid date-picker, mat-datepicker-toggle matSuffix, mat-datepicker; states movies-loading (\"Loading…\"), movies-error (\"Failed to load movies\") with movies-retry-button (\"Retry\"), movie-list with movie-card/movie-title/movie-genre/movie-runtime (\"N min\")/movie-format/screening-button, and movies-empty (\"No screenings on this day\").\n   - apps/cinescope/src/app/movie-list/movie-list.scss (created): layout styles (max-width 960px, card styles, date-field width 220px).\n   - apps/cinescope/src/app/placeholder.ts (created, temporary): empty Placeholder component used for routes 2–5 until later tickets replace them.\n   - apps/cinescope/src/app/app.routes.ts (modified): appRoutes = [ {path:'', pathMatch:'full', component: MovieList}, {path:'screenings/:id/seats', component: Placeholder}, {path:'screenings/:id/summary', component: Placeholder}, {path:'screenings/:id/checkout', component: Placeholder}, {path:'confirmation', component: Placeholder}, {path:'**', redirectTo:''} ].\n   - apps/cinescope/src/app/app.config.ts (modified): providers: provideBrowserGlobalErrorListeners(), provideRouter(appRoutes, withComponentInputBinding()), provideNativeDateAdapter(), provideHttpClient().\n   - Unchanged scaffold: apps/cinescope/src/app/app.ts (App with RouterOutlet), app.html (`<router-outlet />`), app.scss, app.spec.ts, main.ts, styles.scss (Material azure theme, Roboto), index.html (loads Google Fonts render-blocking stylesheet).\n   - /tmp/e2e/cdp.mjs (outside repo): CDP helper (connect creates new tab via /json/new, env CDP_PORT, pins clock to 2026-09-14T10:00, blocks Google Fonts hosts; exports connect, sleep, check). close() is async and closes the tab.\n   - /tmp/e2e/t01.mjs (outside repo): ticket 01 browser checks (AC-02/03/04/49/50/51/52/53/54/55, datepicker, unknown-URL redirect). Not yet passing a full run.\n   - /tmp/e2e/static.mjs (outside repo): static SPA server on port 4200 serving dist/apps/cinescope/browser; running.\n   - /tmp/e2e/dbg*.mjs: throwaway debug scripts.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - `pnpm nx build` aborted by pnpm deps check (ERR_PNPM_ABORTED_REMOVE_MODULES_DIR_NO_TTY). Fix: `export pnpm_config_verify_deps_before_run=false` in each shell command. Did not reinstall because the pnpm store is nearly empty (1.1 MB) and an offline install would break node_modules.\n   - Accidental `cd` into node_modules changed the working directory. Fix: use absolute paths.\n   - `curl`, `pkill`, `python3` not available. Fix: node fetch, /proc scanning, and kill -9 by PID.\n   - Vite dev server showed net::ERR_INSUFFICIENT_RESOURCES and blank pages. Fix: stopped the dev server (nx serve, PIDs 787 and 944; also killed executor PID 1050 holding port 4200) and served the production build statically.\n   - Blank page on load: index.html's render-blocking Google Fonts stylesheet hangs in the offline sandbox, which prevents module bootstrap. Fix (test-side only): Network.setBlockedURLs for fonts.googleapis.com and fonts.gstatic.com in cdp.mjs. index.html was not changed. Possible risk if grader is offline.\n   - Stale Chromium and hung WebSocket sessions. Fix: fresh headless Chromium instances (current on port 9444) and new tab per connect.\n   - Test expectation error: 2026-09-17 has 5 movies, not 3. Fixed in t01.mjs.\n   - json-server stopped responding (killed during cleanup). Restarted with `node node_modules/json-server/lib/cli/bin.js --watch db.json --port 3000` (pnpm api failed due to the pnpm check). Current state: listens on IPv6 ::1 only; 127.0.0.1 and localhost give ECONNREFUSED. Unresolved (see Current Work).\n   - Build warning: initial bundle 604 kB exceeds the 500 kB budget warning (not an error; error threshold is 1 MB). Left unchanged so far.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Solved: build workaround, static serving for reliable browser tests, font-host blocking for offline browser tests, a DevTools-based test harness outside the repo.\n   - Ticket 01 code compiles and `pnpm nx build` succeeds with it (verified via the workaround).\n   - Ongoing: the browser test for ticket 01 has not yet passed because the backend is not reachable on IPv4 localhost:3000 (json-server bound to ::1). Need to restart json-server bound to IPv4 (for example `--host 127.0.0.1`) or otherwise make localhost:3000 reachable, then confirm the app loads movies and rerun t01.mjs.\n   - Also to check: the app's requests to http://localhost:3000 must work in Chromium; json-server runs with CORS.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - (Initial task message, the only user message in this conversation) \"Build the cinema seat-booking web application described in spec/README.md, as the Angular application already set up in this Nx workspace (Nx project `cinescope` in apps/cinescope); its stack is described in spec/stack.md. The work is split into tickets in spec/tickets/; implement them in order. spec/README.md is the complete specification: do not ask any questions, and where it is silent choose the simplest option that satisfies it. Finish only when every ticket is done and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds.\"\n   - Standing environment and attribution instructions from the system context: use pnpm only; do not add dependencies; do not edit db.json by hand; keep port 4200; desktop-only 1280×720 or larger; English text. Commit attribution lines apply only if committing (not requested). Do not commit unless asked.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Restore backend reachability at localhost:3000 for the browser (IPv4) and rerun /tmp/e2e/t01.mjs; fix ticket 01 failures.\n   - Ticket 02: /screenings/:id/seats page (loads screening and movie, header with title \"Choose your seats\", subtitle \"Show Date: …\" via formatShowDate, \"You can reserve up to 10 seats per reservation\", SCREEN bar, 15-row auditorium with aisles, entrance in rows 1–10, accessible seats row 1 cols 10–15, 12 couches in row 15, unavailable rendering, unknown id → redirect '/').\n   - Ticket 03: selection (10-seat cap, couch = 2 seats, toast \"Maximum 10 seats per booking\" via MatSnackBar with a data-testid=\"toast\" component, 4000 ms), colours, legend (Available, Selected, Unavailable, Accessible), selected-seats panel.\n   - Ticket 04: BookingService (sessionStorage), Cancel clears booking, Continue to summary (no-op without seats), summary page (\"Your tickets\", items with movie title, date/time, row, seat/couch description, price, Remove, \"Total: X PLN\", Back, Confirm), prices (25/32/39 PLN; couch 89 PLN), guards for summary and checkout.\n   - Ticket 05: checkout form (\"Your details\", fields with labels and ids per spec 9.4, validation rules and messages, touched semantics, persistence to booking, Back, \"Pay X PLN\", POST /reservations with seats in summary order, Processing…, success → /confirmation, failure toast \"Payment failed. Please try again.\", invalid → toast \"The form contains errors\").\n   - Ticket 06: /confirmation page (\"Payment successful\", \"Your tickets will be sent shortly to <email>\", Continue clears booking and goes to /), confirmation guard (paid booking required).\n   - Ticket 07: full walkthrough against spec section 9 identifiers and section 10 acceptance criteria; `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds.\n   - Tick every checkbox in spec/tickets/01..07 as verified (and Status to done); the tickets README defines done as all boxes ticked plus a successful build.\n   - Replace placeholder.ts usage with real pages and delete placeholder.ts.\n   - Cleanup at the end: delete untracked /workspace/project/.pnpm-store (created by my pnpm invocations); restore db.json via git checkout only if test POSTs changed it (verify with git diff first); stop background processes (json-server, static server, Chromium).\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Testing ticket 01 in the browser. The production build is served by /tmp/e2e/static.mjs on port 4200 and renders correctly (day picker and movie-list states) when the Google Fonts hosts are blocked in the CDP session. The app shows movies-error because the backend is unreachable at localhost:3000. The last checks showed json-server running (log: \"Watching...\") and reachable at [::1]:3000 (HTTP 200), but 127.0.0.1:3000 and localhost:3000 return ECONNREFUSED in Node. Chromium's `localhost` resolution is unverified. Last shell commands: restarted json-server directly with node (node node_modules/json-server/lib/cli/bin.js --watch db.json --port 3000) and probed hosts with node fetch.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Make json-server reachable at localhost:3000 for the browser (restart it bound to 127.0.0.1 or 0.0.0.0, e.g. add `--host 127.0.0.1`, and confirm `fetch('http://localhost:3000/movies')` from Node and the app's requests in Chromium succeed). Then rerun `cd /tmp/e2e && CDP_PORT=9444 timeout 100 node t01.mjs` and fix any failures. After ticket 01 passes, proceed to ticket 02 in order, as the user instructed: \"implement them in order\" and \"Finish only when every ticket is done and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /capture/claude-config/projects/-workspace-project/5dce9b95-c95f-42d9-ad14-7fe0b1984c4e.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5dce9b95-c95f-42d9-ad14-7fe0b1984c4e","uuid":"b6b86e2e-6699-48b9-9c8b-d1d050597012","timestamp":"2026-11-03T15:34:39.401Z","isSynthetic":true}
