{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AQTPTg9568LEBTiUGrvWh5","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/project/spec/tickets/01-movie-list.md has been updated. All occurrences were successfully replaced. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5dce9b95-c95f-42d9-ad14-7fe0b1984c4e","uuid":"15fa6214-cc87-44e1-964a-14f4a11b1d98","timestamp":"2026-11-03T15:35:17.876Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/workspace/project/spec/tickets/01-movie-list.md","oldString":"- [ ] AC-","newString":"- [x] AC-","originalFile":"# 01: Movie list and day picker\n\n**What to build:** A customer opens `/`, picks a day with the day picker (five day buttons and a datepicker), and sees the movies playing that day with their screening times, loaded from the backend, with loading, error and empty states. The selected day lives in the URL. Clicking a screening opens its seat map route. Also sets up the five routes from section 3 (screens 2–5 may be empty placeholders for now) and the redirect of unknown URLs to `/`.\n\n**Specification:** sections 1, 2, 3 (routes), 3.3, 4, 9.1.\n\n**Blocked by:** None (can start immediately).\n\n**Status:** ready\n\n- [ ] AC-01 — Without a chosen date, `/` shows today's screenings: one movie card per movie with a screening today.\n- [ ] AC-02 — Each card shows title, genre, runtime in minutes and format (`PL dubbing` / `PL subtitles`).\n- [ ] AC-03 — Each card renders one button per screening of that movie on the selected day, labelled with the screening time (`HH:mm`), ordered by time.\n- [ ] AC-04 — Clicking a screening button navigates to `/screenings/:id/seats` for that screening id.\n- [ ] AC-49 — While the movie request is in flight, `/` shows a loading indicator and no movie cards.\n- [ ] AC-50 — When the movie request fails, `/` shows `Failed to load movies` and a `Retry` button that re-issues the request.\n- [ ] AC-52 — Above the movie list, the day picker shows `Today` and the next four days by English weekday name, followed by a datepicker; `Today` is selected by default.\n- [ ] AC-53 — Choosing another day shows only the movies with a screening on that day, each with only that day's screenings.\n- [ ] AC-54 — A day without screenings shows `No screenings on this day` and no movie cards.\n- [ ] AC-55 — The selected day is kept in the URL as `?date=YYYY-MM-DD`; opening such a URL selects that day, and a missing, invalid or past date selects today.\n- [ ] AC-51 — Every movie-list identifier in section 9.1 is present with the exact names and values given there.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":8,"oldLines":14,"newStart":8,"newLines":14,"lines":[" "," **Status:** ready"," ","-- [ ] AC-01 — Without a chosen date, `/` shows today's screenings: one movie card per movie with a screening today.","-- [ ] AC-02 — Each card shows title, genre, runtime in minutes and format (`PL dubbing` / `PL subtitles`).","-- [ ] AC-03 — Each card renders one button per screening of that movie on the selected day, labelled with the screening time (`HH:mm`), ordered by time.","-- [ ] AC-04 — Clicking a screening button navigates to `/screenings/:id/seats` for that screening id.","-- [ ] AC-49 — While the movie request is in flight, `/` shows a loading indicator and no movie cards.","-- [ ] AC-50 — When the movie request fails, `/` shows `Failed to load movies` and a `Retry` button that re-issues the request.","-- [ ] AC-52 — Above the movie list, the day picker shows `Today` and the next four days by English weekday name, followed by a datepicker; `Today` is selected by default.","-- [ ] AC-53 — Choosing another day shows only the movies with a screening on that day, each with only that day's screenings.","-- [ ] AC-54 — A day without screenings shows `No screenings on this day` and no movie cards.","-- [ ] AC-55 — The selected day is kept in the URL as `?date=YYYY-MM-DD`; opening such a URL selects that day, and a missing, invalid or past date selects today.","-- [ ] AC-51 — Every movie-list identifier in section 9.1 is present with the exact names and values given there.","+- [x] AC-01 — Without a chosen date, `/` shows today's screenings: one movie card per movie with a screening today.","+- [x] AC-02 — Each card shows title, genre, runtime in minutes and format (`PL dubbing` / `PL subtitles`).","+- [x] AC-03 — Each card renders one button per screening of that movie on the selected day, labelled with the screening time (`HH:mm`), ordered by time.","+- [x] AC-04 — Clicking a screening button navigates to `/screenings/:id/seats` for that screening id.","+- [x] AC-49 — While the movie request is in flight, `/` shows a loading indicator and no movie cards.","+- [x] AC-50 — When the movie request fails, `/` shows `Failed to load movies` and a `Retry` button that re-issues the request.","+- [x] AC-52 — Above the movie list, the day picker shows `Today` and the next four days by English weekday name, followed by a datepicker; `Today` is selected by default.","+- [x] AC-53 — Choosing another day shows only the movies with a screening on that day, each with only that day's screenings.","+- [x] AC-54 — A day without screenings shows `No screenings on this day` and no movie cards.","+- [x] AC-55 — The selected day is kept in the URL as `?date=YYYY-MM-DD`; opening such a URL selects that day, and a missing, invalid or past date selects today.","+- [x] AC-51 — Every movie-list identifier in section 9.1 is present with the exact names and values given there."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":true}}
