{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Build the Cinescope cinema seat-booking app as the Angular 22 project `cinescope` (apps/cinescope) in the Nx workspace at /workspace/project, following spec/README.md and spec/stack.md. Implement tickets 01–07 in spec/tickets in order. Do not ask questions; where the spec is silent, choose the simplest option. Finish only when every ticket's boxes are ticked, each ticket's status is done, and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds. Do not commit unless asked.\n\n   Standing constraints from the user and environment: use pnpm only (no npm or yarn); do not add dependencies; do not hand-edit db.json; keep port 4200; desktop-only (1280×720 or larger); all text in English. Run pnpm/nx commands with `export pnpm_config_verify_deps_before_run=false` first. Use absolute paths.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Angular 22 standalone, zoneless, signals (signal, computed, input, input.required), @for/@if/@switch control flow.\n   - Router with withComponentInputBinding (route params bind to inputs); CanActivateFn guards; `route.paramMap`.\n   - `toObservable` and `takeUntilDestroyed` from @angular/core/rxjs-interop; rxjs switchMap, catchError, EMPTY, forkJoin.\n   - HttpClient against json-server 0.17.4 at http://localhost:3000 (GET /movies, /movies/:id, /screenings, /screenings/:id, POST /reservations).\n   - Angular Material 22: MatButtonModule (mat-flat-button, mat-stroked-button), MatDatepickerModule, MatFormFieldModule, MatInputModule, MatSnackBar (openFromComponent, MAT_SNACK_BAR_DATA), provideNativeDateAdapter.\n   - sessionStorage booking persistence.\n   - Browser verification via a hand-rolled CDP client (/tmp/e2e/cdp.mjs, connect/navigate/evaluate/waitFor/screenshot/close, pins clock to 2026-09-14T10:00, blocks Google Fonts hosts) against headless Chromium at /opt/ms-playwright/chromium-1234/chrome-linux/chrome on port 9444 (profile /tmp/chrome-prof7). The static production server on port 4200 serves dist/apps/cinescope/browser.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - apps/cinescope/src/app/models.ts: Movie, Screening, CustomerDetails, NewReservation, Reservation.\n   - apps/cinescope/src/app/api.ts: CinemaApi with movies(), movie(id), screenings(), screening(id), screeningWithMovie(id) (added in ticket 04: `this.screening(id).pipe(switchMap(s => this.movie(s.movieId).pipe(map(movie => ({screening: s, movie})))))`), createReservation(reservation). BASE_URL = 'http://localhost:3000'.\n   - apps/cinescope/src/app/dates.ts: WEEKDAYS, startOfToday, addDays, toIsoDate, parseIsoDate, formatShowDate(isoDate, time) producing e.g. \"Tuesday 15 Sep 16:00\".\n   - apps/cinescope/src/app/movie-list/movie-list.ts/.html/.scss: ticket 01 movie list and day picker (done, verified 29/29).\n   - apps/cinescope/src/app/app.config.ts: provideBrowserGlobalErrorListeners, provideRouter(appRoutes, withComponentInputBinding()), provideNativeDateAdapter(), provideHttpClient().\n   - apps/cinescope/src/app/app.routes.ts: currently\n     ```ts\n     export const appRoutes: Routes = [\n       { path: '', pathMatch: 'full', component: MovieList },\n       { path: 'screenings/:id/seats', component: SeatSelection },\n       { path: 'screenings/:id/summary', component: Placeholder },\n       { path: 'screenings/:id/checkout', component: Placeholder },\n       { path: 'confirmation', component: Placeholder },\n       { path: '**', redirectTo: '' },\n     ];\n     ```\n     TODO for ticket 04: summary route → Summary with canActivate: [bookingInProgress]; checkout → Placeholder with canActivate: [bookingInProgress]. Import Summary from './summary/summary' and bookingInProgress from './booking/booking'.\n   - apps/cinescope/src/app/placeholder.ts: empty Placeholder component, still used for checkout and confirmation until tickets 05/06; delete when no longer used.\n   - apps/cinescope/src/app/seat-selection/auditorium.ts: types CellKind ('seat'|'couch'|'aisle'|'entrance'), Cell {kind, row, start, end, span, ids, accessible}, AuditoriumRow. Exports seatId(row, col) → `R${row}C${col}`, AUDITORIUM (15 rows; rows 1–10 have an entrance gap span 4 in place of columns 1–4; aisle span 2 between 4|5 and 20|21; row 15 is couches), isSeatLike(cell), bookedCells(seats) (flatMap rows, filter seat-like cells whose ids are all in seats, in row/column order).\n   - apps/cinescope/src/app/seat-selection/seat-selection.ts: SeatSelection (imports MatButtonModule). Input `id = input.required<string>()`. Signals: screening, movie, selected (ReadonlySet<string>). Computed: occupied, showDate, selectedCount, selectedRows (rows with labels 'a' or 'a-b'), rows (cells with state). Constructor: toObservable(id) → switchMap(api.screeningWithMovie(Number(id)) with catchError → router.navigate(['/']) and EMPTY) → sets screening, movie, and selected = new Set(bookings.startOrResume(screening.id).seats). select(cell): ignores when no screening, non-seat-like, or occupied; deselects when all ids are selected; otherwise toasts 'Maximum 10 seats per booking' when size + ids.length > 10; saves via bookings.save({screeningId, seats}). cancel(): bookings.clear(), selected cleared, navigate '/'. continue(): navigates to /screenings/:id/summary when selectedCount > 0. Seat states: stateOf(cell, occupied, selected) returns null for gaps, unavailable if any id occupied, selected if all ids selected, else accessible or available.\n   - apps/cinescope/src/app/seat-selection/seat-selection.html: wraps everything in `@if (screening()) {...}`. Contains seat-map-title, seat-map-subtitle (\"Show Date: …\"), seat-limit-info, screen-indicator \"SCREEN\", seat-map with seat-row/row-label-left/right/seat (button, data-row, data-column, data-state, disabled when unavailable, click→select)/couch (data-column-sta